  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{7}{2},$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{7}{2})\\cup (\\frac{7}{2},\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929417/assets/0369af7512da3b65db27bd9f7945009a3ea15dfbac64cba9cc21adb9c1f19b17.png)",
